course: dictionary
lesson: 3559
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Fence is one of them. Read the words around it to find out which meaning the writer wants. «The dog could not get out because the fence was too high.» The words high and dog tell you a fence is a wall around a garden.
explain: Fence can also be a verb, a doing word. «The farmer will fence in the field» means he will put a fence around it. The little words in and round are clues that the action is about building a barrier.
explain: Fence has a third meaning: a sport where people fight with long thin swords. Try each meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one. If not, try the next meaning.
fact: A fence is a wall of wood, metal or wire around a garden or field.
fact: To fence something in means to put a fence around it.
fact: Fencing is a sport where people fight with long thin swords.
fact: «Sit on the fence» means not choosing a side.
fact: A small hole about 13 centimetres wide, roughly the size of a CD, at the bottom of a fence lets hedgehogs travel between gardens.
exercise: «For example, a girl in London kicks her ball over the fence.» What is the fence here? | A sport with long thin swords | A gate to the park | A hole for hedgehogs | *A wall around a garden
exercise: Mum says, «Don't sit on the fence; tell us what you think.» What does sit on the fence mean? | *Not choose a side | Stay outside all day | Paint it green | Climb up and sit on the top
exercise: Lia goes to fencing club after school. What is fencing? | A game with a ball and a net | A kind of garden hedge | *A sport of fighting with long thin swords | A word for a wooden gate
test:
The farmer wants to fence in the sheep. What does fence in mean? | *To put a fence around | To pick up | To sing loudly | To bake bread
test:
«Climbing fences can break things in the garden and you can get hurt.» What is a fence in this sentence? | A sport | A gate | *A wall of wood, metal or wire around a garden | A row of flowers
exam:
«Mangroves are a wall against storms, like a sponge and a fence in one.» What does a fence do in this sentence? | It is a fish that lives in the sea | *It acts as a wall that blocks something | It is a sport | It is a kind of bird
